      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having some trouble with an iam policy for an s3 bucket. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to it but i keep getting an \"access denied\" error in the cloudwatch logs even though i added the s3:PutObject permission. here is the policy i'm using:\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\ncan u take a look and tell me what i'm missing? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The IAM policy you've created is a good start, but it's a bit too straightforward, not accounting for the nuances of S3 bucket permissions. You're trying to write logs to the bucket, but the issue is likely due to the fact that the `s3:PutObject` permission only grants read access to the bucket, not write access.\n\nTo fix this, you need to add the `s3:PutObject` permission with the `x-amz-roa` (read-only access) attribute set to `false`, which will allow the Lambda function to write to the bucket. Here's an updated policy:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:PutObjectAcl\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\",\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringLike\": {\n          \"aws:SourceArn\": {\n            \"aws:SourceAccount\": \"123456789012\",\n            \"aws:SourceRegion\": \"us-west-2\"\n          }\n        }\n      }",
      "source": "target",
